# Text files are stored and checked out with LF on every machine, whatever
# core.autocrlf is set to (2026-11-22). Directories or files that must keep
# their exact bytes (evidence covered by recorded checksums, executed database
# migrations, vendor deliveries) override this with their own -text or binary
# rules, in this file or in a .gitattributes next to them.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Windows batch files run under cmd.exe and keep CRLF in the working tree.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
